Certificate revocation checks have stopped!

Firezone could not reach the revocation information published by the certificate
authority "<%= @issuer %>", and has stopped trying.

Until this is fixed, devices holding a certificate from this CA are let on even
if the CA has since revoked that certificate. Everything else about the
certificate is still checked, so an expired or untrusted one is still refused.

Below is the last error:

<%= @error_message %>

Details:
  Account: <%= @account.name %>
  Account ID: <%= @account.id %>
  Certificate Authority: <%= @issuer %>
  Address: <%= @endpoint.distribution_point %>
  Last Checked At: <%= @endpoint.crl_fetched_at || @endpoint.ocsp_checked_at || "Never" %>
  Failing Since: <%= @endpoint.errored_at || "Unknown" %>

How to fix it:

  1. Check that the address above is reachable from the public internet, and
     that it is served over http:// or https://. Firezone will not fetch from a
     private or internal address.

  2. Edit and Save the trust anchor this CA belongs to, in your Firezone
     settings, to start checking again:
     <%= @settings_url %>

     Checks resume on the next scheduled run.
